∇
∇PLAY N;S;M;W;A;YOU
⍝ PLAY THE MACHINE: N IS 1 TO MOVE FIRST, AS X, OR 2 TO LET
⍝ IT BEGIN. THE SQUARES ARE 1 TO 9, ROW BY ROW.
YOU←1 ¯1[N]
S←9⍴0
M←1
L:→(M≠YOU)/MINE
SHOW S
S[ASK S]←M
→NEXT
MINE:A←CHOOSE S
'I TAKE ';A
S[A]←M
NEXT:W←OUTCOME S
M←-M
→(W=0)/L
SHOW S
→(W=2)/DRAW
→(W=YOU)/WON
'I WIN.'
→0
WON:'YOU WIN.'
→0
DRAW:'A DRAW.'
∇
∇SHOW S;B
⍝ THE BOARD: X, O, AND A DOT FOR AN EMPTY SQUARE.
B←9 2⍴' '
B[;2]←'O.X'[S+2]
3 6⍴,B
∇
∇R←TRAIN N;K
⍝ FORGET, THEN LEARN FROM N GAMES AGAINST ITSELF. R IS HOW
⍝ MANY X WON, O WON AND WERE DRAWN. EVERY 1000 GAMES IT SAYS
⍝ HOW MANY POSITIONS IT KNOWS, AND THE BYTES STILL FREE.
KEYS←VALS←⍳0
R←0 0 0
K←0
L:R←R+(GAME 0.1)=1 ¯1 2
K←K+1
→(0≠1000|K)/NEXT
'GAMES ';K;'  POSITIONS ';(⍴KEYS);'  FREE ';⎕WA
NEXT:→(K<N)/L
∇
∇R←TRIAL N;K;ME
⍝ N GAMES AS X, THEN N AS O, AGAINST A RANDOM PLAYER. EACH ROW
⍝ OF R IS HOW MANY THE MACHINE WON, LOST AND DREW.
R←2 3⍴0
K←0
L:ME←1-2×K≥N
R[1+K≥N;]←R[1+K≥N;]+(ME AGAINST 0)=ME,(-ME),2
K←K+1
→(K<2×N)/L
∇
∇V←VALUE T;C;N
⍝ WHAT EACH ROW OF T IS WORTH TO THE PLAYER WHO MADE IT.
⍝ A POSITION NOT SEEN BEFORE IS ADDED, WORTH 0.5.
C←CODES T
N←(KEYS⍳C)>⍴KEYS
N←N∧(⍳⍴C)=C⍳C
KEYS←KEYS,N/C
VALS←VALS,0.5+0×N/C
V←VALS[KEYS⍳C]
∇
